SUMMARY OF CHANGES:
============================================================================

Added 2 sections to the TCL script:

1. Lines 7-9: Change to gateware directory
   - Capture the script directory with [file dirname [info script]]
   - Change Vivado's working directory to that location with cd command
   - Enables relative path resolution for init files

2. Lines 21-22: Add init files to project
   - Use add_files command to register init files with the project
   - Target fileset sim_1 (standard simulation fileset that works for synthesis too)
   - Vivado will now copy/include these files in the project

Why This Works:
  • On Windows batch mode, Vivado doesn't automatically set working directory to script location
  • By explicitly using cd + [file dirname [info script]], we ensure the working dir is correct
  • The $readmemh() calls in Verilog now resolve correctly because CWD = gateware directory
  • add_files ensures Vivado tracks the files and includes them in synthesis

No Logic Changes:
  • No changes to memory architecture, sizes, or initialization content
  • Only file path resolution and project file registration
  • Synthesis behavior and netlist output remain identical

